{
  "_comment": [
    "Guise bundled device catalog.",
    "",
    "STRUCTURE: 'socs' holds everything implied by the chip (GPU renderer, platform,",
    "ABI list, codec vendor prefixes, CPU part numbers). 'devices' holds the handset",
    "identity plus a pointer to its SoC. Adding a phone normally means adding six lines",
    "that reference an existing SoC, so the derived values cannot drift apart.",
    "",
    "DATA PROVENANCE - READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A FIELD:",
    "The identity fields (brand, manufacturer, model, product, device, SoC, GPU,",
    "display geometry) reflect shipping configurations and are safe to rely on.",
    "The BUILD METADATA fields (buildId, buildIncremental, securityPatch, buildHost,",
    "buildUser, buildTimeMs) are FORMAT-CORRECT EXAMPLES, not verified dumps -- with one",
    "exception noted below. They are kept honest in three ways: (1) the build fingerprint",
    "is derived from these fields, so it is always internally consistent; (2) the build",
    "ID's version token is realigned to the release the device is actually running, so a",
    "profile used across Android versions does not produce a release/build-ID mismatch;",
    "and (3) the app offers 'Capture this device', which produces a profile from a real",
    "handset with every field verified.",
    "",
    "ONE ENTRY IS A REAL CAPTURE: xiaomi_xaga. Its identity, fingerprint, build ID,",
    "incremental version and build host were read off an actual Redmi Note 11T Pro and",
    "reported by the probe app. Everything else is transcribed.",
    "",
    "Prefer a captured profile. Replace or extend these entries with captures."
  ],
